-- title:
--   Each branch at a crossing is generated by two elements (a,p)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit whose image in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ under `ZMod.unitsMap` is $1$, with $M/p$ nonzero, and assume the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` lies in the field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` obtained by adjoining to $\mathbb{Q}$ the integral form ratios for $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$. Let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` for $X_H(M)$ over $R_p$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and let $\rho : R_p \to A$ be a ring map compatible with the structure map $R_p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with a ring map $\rho_O : R_p \to O$ and maximal ideal generated by $p$, and let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa_A$ satisfy $\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O = \mathrm{residue} \circ \rho$. Write $X_O$ for the base change `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO`, the fibre product of the structure morphism of $X_H(M)$ with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\rho_O$. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two component morphisms `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` and `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 1`, and let $x_n$ be its image in $X_O$ under `crossingPt`. Assume the points `𝔛.ξinf …` and `𝔛.ξzero …` of $X_O$ both specialise to $x_n$. Then the two branch ideals at $x_n$ — the preimages under the specialisation maps on stalks of the maximal ideals of the stalks at `𝔛.ξinf …` and at `𝔛.ξzero …` — are each generated by two elements, one of which is the germ at $x_n$ of the global section of $X_O$ pulled back from $p \in O$: there are $a, b$ in the stalk of $X_O$ at $x_n$ with $(a, p)$ equal to the branch ideal of the first specialisation and $(b, p)$ equal to that of the second.
--
--   At a supersingular crossing point of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_H(M)$ over a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $p$, the local ring looks like two branches meeting transversally; this statement records that each branch ideal becomes principal modulo $p$, with a uniformiser of the base as the second generator. It feeds into [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.forall_exists_orientedEtaleCrossingChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.forall_exists_orientedEtaleCrossingChart), which produces oriented étale charts at crossings.
